  "notes": "ドリブル is borrowed from English \"dribble\" and is common in sports commentary and everyday sports talk.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ドリブルで{抜|ぬ}く: to dribble past someone\n- ドリブル{突破|とっぱ}: dribbling breakthrough\n- ドリブルが{上手|うま}い: to be good at dribbling\n- ドリブルで{仕掛|しか}ける: to make a move while dribbling\n\nSOCCER vs BASKETBALL:\n- Soccer: controlling the ball with the feet while moving forward\n- Basketball: bouncing the ball while moving\n\nIn Japanese sports vocabulary, ドリブル is used the same way in both sports. Context (サッカー or バスケ) clarifies which sport is meant.\n\nRELATED:\n- パス: pass\n- シュート: shot\n- フェイント: feint",
